  "details": "   * SECURITY UPDATE: block environment variable changes from trusted PL/Perl\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2024-10979.patch: block environment variable changes from trusted PL/Perl\n     - CVE-2024-10979\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: restrict access to non-system views and foreign tables during pg_dump\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2024-7348.patch: restrict access to non-system views and foreign tables during pg_dump\n     - CVE-2024-7348\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: prevent int/size_t overflows in libpq\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2025-12818.patch: prevent int/size_t overflows in libpq\n     - CVE-2025-12818\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: restrict psql meta-commands in plain-text dumps (\\restrict/\\unrestrict)\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2025-8714.patch: restrict psql meta-commands in plain-text dumps (\\restrict/\\unrestrict)\n     - CVE-2025-8714\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: harden tsvector/tsquery code against overflows\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-14662.patch: harden tsvector/tsquery code against overflows\n     - CVE-2026-14662\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: fix potential buffer overrun in regexp match/split functions\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-14664.patch: fix potential buffer overrun in regexp match/split functions\n     - CVE-2026-14664\n   * debian/patches/fix-regress-tzdata-LMT.patch: refresh the date,\n     timestamptz and horology expected outputs for tzdata 2024b+, which\n     reports LMT instead of PST for pre-1883 America/Los_Angeles dates",
